@ishaan-jaff As mentioned in email, I think now isn't the right time to integrate with LiteLLM. I'm going to close it to avoid too stale a PR.

For anyone who comes across this, we closed this not because LiteLLM isn't great, but because we made the crazy choice of trying to do on our own many things that LiteLLM does before we knew it existed! LiteLLM has correctly anticipated features that we ended up needing to build even months later. So, _if you are starting your own project using LLMs_, **I recommend using LiteLLM!** It'll save you time early on _and_ down the road.

..and there may come a time where Continue switches to LiteLLM - will open a new PR then!

@bra1nDump This is spotless, nice work! Only improvement I would suggest is instead of changing `npm run esbuild` to use esbuild-base, it might be better to use `esbuild.mjs` as the common denominator. The file includes
